From 3b18db8df9b9a889e4c0563d639af3e0441fe1fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:43:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plugin: saturate the AP MLD capacity before narrowing it to
 maxNumMLDs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On mac80211_hwsim with mlo=1, hwsim advertises an interface-combination
AP limit of 2048 (drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim.c:5268-5277).
wifiGen_rad_supports() (src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c:720) copies that driver
limit, via the uint32_t wld_getMaxNrAPs() (src/wld.c:361, backed by the
uint32_t g_MaxNrAPs global promoted from pRad->maxNrHwBss at
src/wld.c:512-517), into wld_mldCapa_t.maxNumMLDs, which is a uint8_t
(include/wld/wld_mld.h:90). 2048 truncates to 0 there.

wld_mld_updateMldCapa() (src/wld_mld.c:899) keeps the max of the stored
and the new candidate per MLD group (src/wld_mld.c:904-909), so a zero
candidate from a later radio callback cannot lower an already-retained
AP capacity, but the very first radio still computes its candidate
before wld.c:512-517 promotes g_MaxNrAPs, so it observes the stale
initial default (4, src/wld.c:136) rather than the true driver limit.
The AP MLD group capacity therefore stays at 4, and
s_updateGlobalMaxNumMlds() (src/wld_mld.c:850-855) exports
Radio.*.Capabilities.MaxNumMLDs = min(STD_MAX_NUM_MLDS=25,
AP capacity 4 + EP capacity 3) = 7 with pwhm-patches/0007 applied
(4, without it), instead of reflecting hwsim's real, much larger,
interface budget.

Saturate the driver-reported value to the destination type's maximum
before the narrowing assignment, the same way an out-of-range driver
value is normally clamped, instead of letting it silently wrap to 0.
wld_getMaxNrAPs() is the only call site assigning into a
wld_mldCapa_t.maxNumMLDs field with a driver-scale (non-constant)
value, so this is the only narrowing site to guard; the EP path
(src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c:760,787) assigns wld_getMaxNrEPs(), which is
only ever the compile-time MAXNROF_RADIO default (3) and is never
promoted by a driver limit, so it cannot overflow.

With this fix, and replaying the callback-before-global-update order
against hwsim's advertised limit (2048 for every radio once promoted,
uint8-saturated to 255) plus pwhm-patches/0007's EP capacity of 3:
AP group capacity saturates to 255, EP group stays 3, and
Radio.*.Capabilities.MaxNumMLDs = min(25, 255 + 3) = 25.

Not built, not booted; verified with the toolchain's
x86_64-openwrt-linux-musl-gcc -std=gnu99 -fPIC -Wall -Wextra -Werror
-fsyntax-only against src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c, and pwhm-patches/0001-0009
apply in order (git apply --check) on a pristine pwhm-v7.29.20 tree.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c
index 59e8bdcd1caf..9cbad16ec525 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_rad.c
@@ -716,8 +716,12 @@ int wifiGen_rad_supports(T_Radio* pRad, char* buf _UNUSED, int bufsize _UNUSED)
             /*
              * When APMLO is supported, all BSSs can be set as SLOs
              * which defines maxNumAPMLDs to maxBSSs that can be created by the wiphy device
+             *
+             * wld_getMaxNrAPs() is a uint32_t driver-reported limit (e.g. mac80211_hwsim
+             * advertises 2048), while wld_mldCapa_t.maxNumMLDs is a uint8_t: saturate to
+             * UINT8_MAX before the assignment narrows it, instead of silently wrapping to 0.
              */
-            apMldCapa.maxNumMLDs = wld_getMaxNrAPs();
+            apMldCapa.maxNumMLDs = SWL_MIN(wld_getMaxNrAPs(), (uint32_t) UINT8_MAX);
             apMldCapa.maxNumLinksPerMLD = wiphyInfo.extCapas.maxNumSimultenousLinks[WLD_WIPHY_IFTYPE_AP] + 1;
 
             pRad->cap.apCap7.tidLinkMapNegotiation = (pRad->cap.tidLinkMapCapability != TID_LINK_MAP_CAPABILITY_NOT_SUPPORTED);
